 # Chert connector relay
 
-Implemented, private, not deployed. This Node service transports JSON signaling only; customer LiveKit media never traverses it. The control-plane database owns authorization, activation, connection generations, call pins, decisions, sealed credentials and delivery acknowledgements.
+Private connector relay; pilot deployment evidence is tracked separately from media readiness. This Node service transports JSON signaling only; customer LiveKit media never traverses it. The control-plane database owns authorization, activation, connection generations, call pins, decisions, sealed credentials and delivery acknowledgements.
 
 Use Node 22.23.2 or 24.14.0. `npm ci --ignore-scripts`, `npm run check`, `npm test`, then `npm start`. No Docker is required. Railway service root is `connector-relay/`; `railway.json` supplies the start command and process health check. Set `RAILPACK_NODE_VERSION=24.14.0`, `CHERT_CONTROL_ORIGIN=https://<control-plane-host>`, a generated secret-manager `CHERT_CONNECTOR_RELAY_SECRET` (at least 32 random characters), and the platform-provided `PORT`. Configure the same relay secret on the control plane. Preserve existing control-plane Supabase, credential pepper and destination encryption keys. Never place secret values in flags, logs or this repository.
 
 Expose this service only through the platform HTTPS/WSS ingress. The application port is HTTP behind that ingress. `/healthz` proves process liveness, not control-plane authorization. Public endpoints are `/connect` (WebSocket), `/inspect` and `/reconcile` (POST). Browser Origin-bearing upgrades are rejected. Credential-bearing redirects are forbidden. Frame/body size is 32 KiB; a socket allows at most eight concurrent client operations and bounded buffered output. Management RPCs have a two-second transport timeout. A disconnected response never proves a decision failed; recover through reconciliation.
 
-The relay polls the authenticated internal control-plane route every 200 ms while connected; the database lease lasts five seconds. Every connection acquires a new persisted generation. Multiple processes may run, but the most recent connection fences older ones. A state change from standby/active closes the socket; the supervised CLI restarts, reconciles and receives its new role. Recovery-only connections remain draining. Deliveries replay until durable acknowledgement. A receipt is retired from delivery after an owned lifecycle acknowledgement; authoritative receipts remain in the call row. No cleanup assertion is inferred from that acknowledgement: local journals and adapter receipts remain the cleanup authority.
+The relay polls the authenticated internal control-plane route every 200 ms while connected; the database lease lasts five seconds. A transient network failure, timeout, HTTP 429 or HTTP 5xx during polling receives at most one retry after 100 ms, within the last confirmed lease measured conservatively from request start. Each request remains bounded to two seconds or the shorter remaining lease. Authorization rejection and malformed responses close immediately; decisions and connection acquisition are never automatically replayed. No frames are forwarded while a poll is unavailable. Poll failures emit only a fixed category, action and numeric status, never credentials or response bodies. Every connection acquires a new persisted generation. Multiple processes may run, but the most recent connection fences older ones. A state change from standby/active closes the socket; the supervised CLI restarts, reconciles and receives its new role. Recovery-only connections remain draining. Deliveries replay until durable acknowledgement. A receipt is retired from delivery after an owned lifecycle acknowledgement; authoritative receipts remain in the call row. No cleanup assertion is inferred from that acknowledgement: local journals and adapter receipts remain the cleanup authority.
 
 This is a bounded first-pilot implementation, not a high-volume relay benchmark. Request/DB load, ingress throttling, monitoring and secret rotation need deployment review. Retention intentionally favors recovery; no automated deletion of call pins, receipts or recovery credentials is provided. See [operations](../docs/operations/CONNECTORS.md).
+
+The relay emits a `chert-authority-v1` WebSocket ping after a successful authority
+poll, at most once per second. Updated connectors terminate a socket after five
+seconds without this marker, including sockets left open by intermediaries.
+A timer or ordinary traffic never generates this marker. It indicates transport
+freshness only; per-call authorization and media readiness remain independent.
+Deploy this relay before upgrading connectors that require the heartbeat.
